{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The only chat entry on this trip, MSG-00102-001 in the chat log, is a message from the DRIVER - 'boss BKE quite jam, i go Upper Bukit Timah ok?' - sent at 11:29:04, roughly six minutes after the vehicle had already been moving (started 11:23:30); the rider never replied, the message merely being read at 11:29:40. POL-RD-04 exonerates a deviation only to the extent it is attributable to a rider instruction, and a driver's own proposal is not a rider instruction, so the clause's limb (a) fails at the outset. With waypoint_hint null on that message, the clause's corroboration limb cannot be run either: POL-RD-04 is unavailable and the diversion is left wholly unexplained by anything the rider did.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00102", "EV-TRIP-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "payload.messages[0].sender",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's entire defence is a traffic event on the BKE near Dairy Farm, and no advisory in the pool supports it. I disclose that EV-ADVIS-00102-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0, and fired the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; its issue detail records that no LTA advisory covers the BKE or the Upper Bukit Timah corridor in the 11:16-11:55 window. I rely on that absence itself, which is citable. POL-RD-03 exonerates a deviation only where a traffic_advisory names a road or expressway segment the optimal route traverses and carries a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle would have reached it; no such advisory exists here, so nothing on this record excuses the longer route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00102-01", "EV-CHAT-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the only defence pleaded is a traffic event asserted with no traffic_advisory anywhere in the pool - EV-ADVIS-00102-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and does not cover the trip window - POL-RD-10(5) is engaged: an exculpatory basis is asserted against an artifact that is not in the pool. Escalation is mandatory and terminal under that clause, and it holds the disputed SGD 7.00 rather than letting the present charged state stand, which is the only relief this record can give the rider. The full case summary, both briefs and the admissibility report should go to the reviewer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00102-01", "EV-CHAT-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I am straight about the arithmetic rather than stretching it: the fully unimpaired track - 193 fixes, 10 s sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps - puts the traced distance at 21.79 km against the 20.4 km optimal, an excess of 1.39 km, which is 6.81%. That excess is real and cleanly measured, but it falls short of POL-RD-01's 20% establishment limb, so no deviation is established on this record and I do not press a POL-RD-02 recomputation, which by its terms runs only on an established deviation. That is exactly why the rider's route here is escalation under POL-RD-10(5), which holds the money, rather than a partial refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00102", "EV-TRIP-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's congestion account cites no evidence ID at all - no advisory, no gantry, no artifact - and POL-RD-08 provides that a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the driver, and that assertions from either side citing no evidence ID carry no weight and are discarded. The rider's version, by contrast, is pinned to this trip's own artifacts: the trip record, the gps trace and the fare breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-00102, so the identity requirement of POL-RD-08(a) is satisfied and this dispute is decided on this trip's evidence rather than on anyone's say-so.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00102", "EV-TRIP-00102", "EV-GPS-00102", "EV-FARE-00102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "RIDER and DRIVER: this is decided on the trip's own instruments, and the outcome is NO_ACTION — the $29.91 metered charge stands and no refund issues.\n\nWhy. POL-RD-01 establishes a route deviation only if the excess over the optimal route is BOTH more than 20% of optimal AND more than 0.8 km. The governing measurement is the GPS trace distance of 21.79 km (EV-GPS-00102), which POL-RD-01 makes govern over the rounded 21.8 km trip-record convenience copy. The booked optimal is 20.4 km (EV-TRIP-00102). Excess = 1.39 km, which is 6.81% of optimal. The absolute limb passes (1.39 km > 0.8 km), but the percentage limb fails badly (6.81% is far below 20%). Both limbs must pass, so no deviation is established, and POL-RD-01 then directs NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. The rider's own advocate accepted this arithmetic and did not press a POL-RD-02 recomputation, which by its terms runs only on an established deviation.\n\nThe trace cannot be attacked and needs no corroboration. It carries 193 fixes at a steady 10-second interval over 100% coverage, with no gaps, no jumps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds, so the impairment limbs (a)–(c) of POL-RD-07 do not fire.\n\nOn the rider's escalation argument (POL-RD-10(5)): I do not accept it. POL-RD-10(5) escalates where an exculpatory clause is invoked against an artifact that is missing from the pool. The driver does not invoke POL-RD-03 here — the driver's account is that the BKE was crawling and the alternative was 'same distance more or less', i.e. that there was no material deviation, not that a deviation should be excused — and exoneration under POL-RD-03 is only ever reached once a deviation is established under POL-RD-01, which none is. A bare assertion that traffic was bad, with no advisory ID, is what POL-RD-08 speaks to: it does not discharge the driver — but the burden never shifted to the driver, so nothing turns on it. The absence of a traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00102-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is citable and I have considered it; it changes nothing here, because there is no established deviation to excuse.\n\nThe single chat message (EV-CHAT-00102), 'boss BKE quite jam, i go Upper Bukit Timah ok?', is from the driver, not the rider, so POL-RD-04 gives no rider-instruction exoneration, and its waypoint_hint is null so the corroboration limb could not be run in any event. On billing: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00102) charges no ERP gantry and no airport surcharge and its lines reconcile to the $29.91 total to the cent, so POL-RD-09(4) gives the rider nothing. POL-RD-06's driver-pattern check is not engaged because there is no material deviation; in any case deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 640 completed trips in 90 days, so no adverse pattern attaches.\n\nConfidence is 0.90. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact (EV-GPS-00102, EV-TRIP-00102, EV-FARE-00102) sits at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02 cap is 1.0 and the 0.70 escalation floor is not approached. No clause produces a referral."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
